  "text": "This is a comprehensive mapping of how repositories are currently passed through the codebase layers. Key patterns to understand for the refactor:\n\n1. **Most services receive multiple specific repos** - they explicitly depend on many repository types\n2. **Application class holds repos as optional properties** but factory always passes them\n3. **Workflows also receive specific repos** - they don't get an abstraction layer\n4. **Database is always passed alongside repos** - sometimes both are needed\n5. **Factories create repos then pass them to services** - tight coupling point\n\nThe refactor should likely:\n- Create some kind of abstract access layer or repository manager\n- Pass a single \"data access\" object instead of 5+ repos\n- Keep Database instance separate (it's low-level)\n- Or use a Service Locator pattern with the Application itself",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes",
    "Repository Parameterization Analysis"
  ],
